================================================================================
Required external runtime engine — NOT bundled
================================================================================

manga-image-translator (https://github.com/zyddnys/manga-image-translator)
  License: GPL-3.0
  Role: detection, OCR, inpainting, typesetting of manga pages.
  Integration: invoked as an external subprocess (CLI) or HTTP server.
  msrt does not import its modules and does not redistribute its source
  code or container images.

================================================================================
Python dependencies (installed via the user's package manager)
================================================================================

LiteLLM (https://github.com/BerriAI/litellm) — MIT
  Role: OpenAI-compatible proxy that routes to Anthropic, OpenAI, Google
  and other providers.

Typer (https://github.com/fastapi/typer) — MIT
  Role: CLI framework.

Pydantic / pydantic-settings (https://github.com/pydantic/pydantic) — MIT
  Role: configuration, data models.

Rich (https://github.com/Textualize/rich) — MIT
  Role: progress bars, structured terminal output.

structlog (https://www.structlog.org) — Apache-2.0 / MIT
  Role: structured logging.

HTTPX (https://www.python-httpx.org) — BSD-3-Clause
  Role: async HTTP client for the downloader.

Playwright for Python (https://github.com/microsoft/playwright-python) — Apache-2.0
  Role (v0.2+): browser automation for site adapters.

img2pdf (https://gitlab.mister-muffin.de/josch/img2pdf) — LGPL-3.0
  Role (v0.1+, optional): image → PDF packaging.

Pillow (https://python-pillow.org) — HPND
  Role: image manipulation in custom post-processing.

PyYAML (https://github.com/yaml/pyyaml) — MIT
  Role: configuration loading.

Pyphen (https://github.com/Kozea/Pyphen) — GPL-2.0+/LGPL-2.1+/MPL-1.1
  Role (v0.6, optional): Italian hyphenation in custom typesetting.
  When enabled, please review LGPL/MPL obligations before redistributing.

================================================================================
Fonts
================================================================================

msrt does NOT bundle any font. The CLI flag --font-path lets the user
provide their own font file (typically OFL-licensed, e.g. Comic Neue OFL,
Open Sans, Noto Sans). The README documents recommended OFL fonts and
their respective licenses.
